# capture.py regenerates every fixture and every intermediate from the vips
# binary alone, so the whole tree here is reproducible with
# `python3 capture.py` and no Rust toolchain.
#
# fixtures/ IS pinned: analyzeload is load-only, so a port has no way to
# produce these inputs for itself and needs them checked in. They are 82
# tiny files, about 16K in total.
#
# outputs/ holds the intermediate `.v` files every direct `vips analyzeload`
# call writes, and is pure scratch.
outputs/
